"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-19/omp-19/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/6e66a13a8fa112148a94c97b17706eed8dc1d73b/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed the bug: `to_cents` in `ledger/currency.py` was losing a cent on some prices. All the tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and `tests/test_report.py` now pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran each test function directly with `python3`.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` computed `int(amount * 100)`. Floats can't store most decimal prices exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.999\u2026`, and `int()` cuts it down to `1998`. The same happened to `0.29` and `4.35`. That broke the subtotal checks and pushed the 10%-discount total off by one. The tax and discount code was fine.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts the amount to text first, turns that into an exact decimal, multiplies by 100 and rounds to the nearest cent (halves go away from zero). Converting through text means the value is the number as written, like `19.99`, not the float's slightly-off binary version. A spot check gives `19.99\u21921999`, `0.29\u219229`, `4.35\u2192435`, `1.005\u2192101`, `-2.675\u2192-268`, `10\u21921000`.\n\nTwo behaviour changes to be aware of:\n- Amounts with more than two decimal places used to be truncated and are now rounded (`1.005` used to give `100` and now gives `101`).\n- Negative half-cent amounts round away from zero (`-2.675` gives `-268`).\n\nPrices are still stored as floats in `Line.unit_price`. Passing `Decimal` values or strings in from the start would avoid float error altogether. That's a bigger API change, so I didn't make it.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 25470, "requests_cache_write": 36320, "requests_cost_usd": 0.22109399999999998, "requests_count": 4, "requests_input_uncached": 10, "requests_output": 1718, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 0, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T03:24:36.009063+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 21.15, "t_checker_s": 0.383, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1728, "tokens_cache_read": 25470, "tokens_cache_write": 36320, "tokens_fresh": 1728, "tokens_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_main_cache_read": 25470, "tokens_main_cache_write": 36320, "tokens_main_calls": 4, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_main_output": 1718, "tokens_output": 1718, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 25470, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 36320, "tokens_proxy_calls": 4, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_proxy_output": 1718, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 1, "ts_iso": "2026-10-12T20:24:36", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 4, "usage_raw": [{"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 14613, "cost": {"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "input": 0, "output": 0, "total": 0}, "input": 4, "output": 122, "to